Z||000009||88formula||07-11-2001||05:09 PM||||The reason why hypereutectic pistons make more power on a street engine than the same motor with forged pistons is because hypereutectic pistons run with much tighter piston to bore clearances. With tighter piston to bore clearances the rings do a better job of sealing so there is less blow-by.  Ask any competent performance engine builder this and I think most will agree.<P>The competition Cams are good camshafts but the Crane H-260-2 camshaft is a split duration camshaft and makes better use of the fiero’s intake and exhaust system in my opinion. Here are the numbers from Dyno2000.<P>Engine modifications include 2.8-liter engine with Ported manifolds and high flow exhaust, stock heads, 9.5-1 compression, and .020’ over bore. <P>Crane H-260-2 camshaft with 204/216 duration measured @ .050” intake and exhaust.<P>RPM HORSEPOWER TORQUE<P>2000 61.079754 160.334351<BR>2500 80.074005 168.155411<BR>3000 103.449127 181.035965<BR>3500 124.212845 186.319260<BR>4000 142.100525 186.506943<BR>4500 154.616943 180.386429<BR>5000 162.906570 171.051910<BR>5500 165.336563 157.821274<BR>6000 161.043091 140.912704<BR>6500 150.207642 121.321556<P>Comp Cams High energy 252H with 206/206 duration measured @ .050” intake and exhaust.<P>2000 68.787971 180.568420<BR>2500 88.707870 186.286530<BR>3000 111.378136 194.911743<BR>3500 129.259567 193.889343<BR>4000 144.471466 189.618805<BR>4500 152.631042 178.069550<BR>5000 153.040344 160.692368<BR>5500 147.078415 140.393036<BR>6000 134.559402 117.739471<BR>6500 118.006844 95.313217<P>Comp Cams High energy 260 with 212/212 duration measured @ .050” intake and exhaust.<P>2000 65.394119 171.659561<BR>2500 84.694267 177.857956<BR>3000 107.801796 188.653152<BR>3500 127.778130 191.667191<BR>4000 144.944580 190.239761<BR>4500 156.370163 182.431854<BR>5000 161.182419 169.241547<BR>5500 158.313538 151.117462<BR>6000 148.910172 130.296402<BR>6500 134.624329 108.735031<P>Performance with a a five speed fiero that weighs 2925 lbs. with driver. Elevation is 800 feet, temperature 75f, humidity 60%, barometer 29.05. Shift points are as follows, launch rpm 2500 rpm, 1-2 @ 6000 rpm, 2-3 @ 6000 rpm, and 3-4 @ 6000 rpm.   <P>Crane PowerMax 0-60 mph in 6.8 seconds and the quarter mile in 14.94 seconds @ 90.8 mph.<BR>Comp Cams H252 0-60 mph in 7 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.1 @ 88.7 mph.<BR>Comp Cams H260 0-60 mph in 6.8 seconds and the quarter mile in 14.94 seconds @ 90.3 mph.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
